{"Context is created with d.Log instead of the log that includes name/kind/method, causing downstream storage calls to miss those fields - should use log for request-scoped logging": 0.96610027551651, "On storage create error, legacy duration is recorded instead of storage duration, causing storage latency/error metrics to be wrong - should use recordStorageDuration": 0.9950162768363953, "recordStorageDuration is called with name instead of options.Kind, creating high-cardinality metrics with one label value per object name - should use options.Kind": 0.9790523648262024, "The async legacy delete-collection path records storage duration instead of legacy duration, so legacy failures won't show up in legacy metrics - should use recordLegacyDuration": 0.9961103796958923, "The async legacy write uses the request-scoped ctx which gets canceled when the request finishes, causing the goroutine to be canceled immediately and the legacy write never happens - should use a non-canceling base context": 0.9166600108146667, "Legacy update reuses the original objInfo which is often stateful/non-idempotent and may produce a different object on second call - should use the result from storage update wrapped appropriately": 0.9321591258049011}